KZ3 patch 2168 (ENHANCEMENT, experimental): publish generic temporal-upscaler inputs from the live renderer.

The renderer exposes draw and scene-writeback metadata through optional callbacks. Ports own all game-specific
recognition and return only generic actions: jitter this draw, snapshot this depth, capture after this draw, or
suppress host AA before writeback. Command-list and resource handles remain opaque at the interface boundary; no
KZ3 offsets or pass rules are compiled into ps3recomp.

The selected depth is snapshotted immediately after its draw. Presentation supplies that current-frame snapshot
and jitter through rsx_upscale, evaluates before scan-out gamma, and safely restores resource states. Temporal
requests use bilinear output geometry and explicit bilinear fallback even when the user selected Nearest. Failed
upscaled blits fall back to the original image, and incompatible resources are never passed to CopyResource.

Backend changes drain prior GPU work, all shutdown paths destroy the active context, and frame completion resets
the interface's pre-HUD state. These hooks are shared by the port-owned FSR 3.1 adapter and a later XeSS backend.

